# Group buses: strips summed on a bus with its own level, inserts and sends
# (sound-design.md, strip, group, master). Both drum machines go to group 1,
# a compressed drum bus; bass and keys go to group 2, a lightly driven music
# bus; both buses go on to group 3, so one fader rides the band (a group goes
# only to a higher one). A snapshot mutes the drum bus for the break, an auto
# fades the music bus in.
tempo 124
track kit drums Tr909 Kit909
track perc drums Tr808 Kit808
track bass synth Sh101 Sh101Bass
track keys synth Dx7 FmElectricPiano
strip kit: Out group1
strip perc: Level 0.7, Pan 0.3, Out group1
strip bass: Out group2
strip keys: Level 0.7, Send2 0.3, Out group2
group 1 drums: Level 0.9, I1Type Comp, Out group3
group 2 music: Level 0.8, I1Type Overdrive, I1A 0.3, Out group3
group 3 band: Level 0.9

clip beat = kit /16
  bd x...x...x...x...
  cp ....x.......x...
  oh ..x...x...x...x.
clip congas = perc /16
  lc x..x..x...x.x...
  hc ..x...x..x....x.
clip low = bass
  "c2 ~ c2 [eb2 c2] ~ c2 g1 ~"
clip chords = keys voicing
  "<c3:m7 ab2:maj7 f2:m7 g2:7>"
auto fade = group2.Level ramp 0 0.8 /8
snapshot cut: group1.Mute 1
snapshot back: group1.Mute 0
scene intro 8: beat congas low chords fade [back]
scene main 8: beat congas low chords [back]
scene break 4: beat congas low chords [cut]
scene drop 8: beat congas low chords [back]
arrange intro main break drop
